ng and hissing and  or when ace is coming out to the ring  like it's just it's just a different  it's just a different feeling it doesn't  it doesn't require a lot of acting it  really doesn't except  except for me where i  i've got this big smile inside and this  look of disdain outside  they all cheer for me the cheer for the  character the character i play character  i created alexander it's so fun because  we see ace in quite a few vests but  they're very different than your viking  vest they're a lot less furry what was  that like for you to kind of embody  this  like guy who wants to be loved so badly  and and how are you liking the eyeliner  you know the eyeliner was actually my  choice i i thought it was it was pretty  fun and rock and roll yeah you know just  this whole experience with this show has  been so tremendous like even and i fell  in love with these scripts the second  they were sent to us and um it's it's  it's an actor's dream to get to play  because it's limitless this world is so  colorful and the second you put on these  outfits and you walk out into the ring  and as stephen said they're playing your  music and the audience is cheering i  mean you're there you're in it and um i  mean it's just been truly just an  incredible experience to be able to go  from one show that you're really really  proud of to another is um  it's just you know at the end of the day  we're storytellers and just so great to  tell a story that we're so proud of  ace can succeed at the highest level  it's a natural it's in his blood i  imagine the training for this show is a  whole different game for both of you  guys steven obviously you trained for  more than eight seasons to play oliver  queen on arrow what was the difference  of stepping into the ring for heels  versus stepping out to save star city on  arrow well on arrow  everyone was really left to their own  left to their own devices which  um  you know could get complicated if if my  schedule was really was really busy and  they weren't baking in the time for for  training whereas with heels right from  the get-go they built us a gym  and  they they baked in the training time so  you know it actually  while it was a while it was a lot more  physically demanding it was  easier to  stay in shape and feel good because  that everything was everything was baked  into your schedule so steven's had some  experience wrestling i never had any so  i i've had the fortune of working with  some of the greatest heels of all time  randomly like dwayne johnson or adam  copeland and i leaned on adam a lot  actually who who was ed she was a hall  of fame wrestler about you know what  exactly i should be doing but basically  it's unlike anything i've ever done  before it was without a doubt the most  extensive training i've done for  anything  um  and my respect for these men and women  who literally put their lives on the  line every single night to put on a show  and provide for their families um  it's just it's just tenfold since i  began and we we had people we could lean  on but we knew that we had to do right  by the wrestling community and  we know that people like we knew this  show was great the story is awesome  we're so proud of these characters but  we wanted the wrestling community to  watch this and go wow these guys really  put in the work and that was just a lot  of training uh you know if you weren't  in the gym you were in the ring um and  it was just this constant repetition  for eight months um  while covid was a thing so it was even  just it was just a surreal experience  yeah you were putting in a lot of work  but like yet somehow you've been finding  time for your music  [Music]  and it's been so fun to see that on your  instagram and then here we go episode  two ace goes to walk up on the stage for  karaoke and i'm like they're merging  these worlds it's so great and he starts  singing and i'm like that is not the  voice i was expecting  what are the chances that in season one  we could see ace actually croon a little  eight aces in the singer  and apparently jack is because here we  go in episode three yeah yeah  that's right maybe david can you can you  can you can you give us one really  quickly nice little uh when the times  are tough  [Music]  we got kids to come to the show ace  what's the matter do you afraid i'm  gonna go off script even have you shown  mavi any of your wrestling scenes this  whole show is not appropriate for her  yet but have you shown her snippets oh  yeah yeah yeah yeah she's seen  oh gosh she's seen three episodes what i  think and um  you know she she just knows that if um  she just knows that  if wild bills on the screen and or ace  and crystal are on the screen  that it's uh it's time it's time to  cover the eyes that's it  the full eye cover that's you know it's  like whatever i love the fact that we  did get to see cass in a couple episodes  of arrow what are the chances we'll get  a cast cameo in heels i don't know um  that would be fun yeah i'm more we i'm  more interested in the uh in the lauren  ludwig cameo that we get in episode two  break it down how did that happen  my i almost broke up with me i  because with kovid you can't bring  people on to set yeah okay i'm gonna  sign her up as an extra she'll get  tested and she'll be able to come on set  and see what we do she's never seen  anything like this um  and of course it's a 14-hour day and  she's just like alexander like if she  hates being in front of the camera she's  like i'm going to leave you if you do  this again  which scene was she in he's a bartender  in uh in in  an episode  so when you're yelling at someone  because you want more whiskey you're  yelling at your wife yeah exactly  [Music]

